         "notes": "## Summary\nThe team settled Pro plan pricing and the trial length.\n\n## Key Points\n- Three price points were tested: $10, $12 and $15 per seat.\n- Churn in the survey group roughly doubled above $12.\n\n## Decisions\n- Pro plan is priced at $12 per seat per month.\n- The free trial becomes 14 days instead of 7.\n\n## Action Items\n- Marcus: update the pricing page with the $12 price and 14-day trial by Friday the 14th.\n- Me: get legal to review the new trial terms before the pricing page is published.\n"},
        {"id": "wp-action-incident", "kind": "workprompt", "gate": "W1", "expect": "prompts", "title": "API outage retro",
         "notes": "## Summary\nRetro for the 47-minute API outage on Tuesday caused by an expired TLS certificate on the internal load balancer.\n\n## Key Points\n- The expiry alert went to an email list nobody reads.\n\n## Decisions\n- Certificate expiry alerts move to PagerDuty starting this week.\n\n## Action Items\n- Kim: automate certificate renewal with cert-manager.\n- Me: write the public postmortem by Friday.\n- Team: audit the other 12 certificates this week.\n"},
        {"id": "wp-noaction-status", "kind": "workprompt", "gate": "W2", "expect": "none", "title": "Weekly status",
         "notes": "## Summary\nRoutine weekly status round. Everyone shared what they finished; nothing new was decided and no follow-ups were assigned.\n\n## Key Points\n- Ana said the queue migration finished last week and has been stable since.\n- Ben mentioned the billing dashboard has been live for a month with no incidents.\n- The team chatted about the office move and the holiday schedule.\n\n## Decisions\n- None.\n\n## Action Items\n- None.\n"}
      ]
